`--depth=2` lists the files in the argument and one directory level down, and summarizes each directory two levels down with every file below it (`src/deep/b.ts` included); the trailing `/` of `pkg/` doesn't appear in the display paths.
== args
--depth=2
pkg/
== file pkg/top.md
# Top
== file pkg/core/index.ts
export const a = 1;
== file pkg/core/src/a.ts
export const a = 1;
== file pkg/core/src/deep/b.ts
export const b = 2;
export const c = 3;
== stdout
glob view: pkg/
pkg/core/index.ts (1 line): (no header available)
pkg/core/src/ (2 files, 3 lines)
pkg/top.md (1 line): # Top
== stderr
== exit 0
